# L §6.1 What same does: a thing's entries are facts read from both sides together; "on a day on which the two sides'
# entries into one kind disagree, whatever depends on the thing being alive there is a HOLE-SAME hole". a enters ola
# and later ends its life on 2026-06-30 (a replace, L §6.2 "something that ends"); b's entry stands open. On
# 2026-03-01 both sides hold ola (1); on 2026-08-01 they disagree (an unknown member, a hole naming both); lifespan(),
# which depends on the entries, is that hole too, first differing on 2026-07-01 (L §5.7, §8.1).
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "a.tally" sha256 "bb56824a5aca7f9185dfc1255e11d4da6c4b8b3b044fb180ca5d639d13f30922"
  use b = "b.tally" sha256 "847931b0631c7765e9218d2ba25e87830008e77ebc206f92a3fe563bae5c188f"
  same a.persons = b.persons
  same a.ola = b.ola

source s "ustalenia"

input d1: date
input d2: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  d1 = 2026-03-01
  d2 = 2026-08-01

ask mar: count(p in a.persons on d1)
ask aug: count(p in a.persons on d2)
ask life: lifespan(a.ola).from
=== a.tally
model a
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

kind persons

version v1
  cite s
  known 2025-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 2026-01-01..

version v2
  cite s
  known 2025-02-01
  replace persons + [ola] lives 2026-01-01..2026-06-30
=== b.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

kind persons

version v
  cite s
  known 2025-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 2026-01-01..
=== expect
aug: ?"a.ola and b.ola are one, but the entry into a.persons differs on 2026-08-01: 2026-01-01..2026-06-30 (a.v2) and 2026-01-01.. (b.v)" (a.ola, b.ola)
  cut 2026-10-20
life: ?"a.ola and b.ola are one, but the entry into a.persons differs on 2026-07-01: 2026-01-01..2026-06-30 (a.v2) and 2026-01-01.. (b.v)" (a.ola, b.ola)
  cut 2026-10-20
mar: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
